                <pb facs="0195" n="87" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg87"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 112— Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Decree No. 1617 of the 25th of December, 1893—Prolongs
                        to the 31st of January next the state of siege declared by decree No. 1602
                        of November 29, 1893.</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#flush">The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vice-President of the Republic
                        of the United States of Brazil</hi>:</p>
                <p>Seeing that the serious internal disturbance that led to the suspension of the
                    constitutional guaranties in certain parts of the territory of the Republic has
                    not yet ceased, resolves by the terms of article 80 of the constitution to
                    prolong up to January 31 next the state of siege in which, by decree No. 1602 of
                    November 29 last, were declared the federal district and the States of
                    Pernambuco, Rio de Janeiro, São Paulo, Parana, Santa Catharina, and Rio Grande
                    do Sul.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName>Capital federal</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian brazilian-republic" when="1893-12-25">December 25,
                            1893, fifth of the Republic</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/><signed>
                        <list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Floriano Peixoto</hi>,</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cassiano do Nascimento.</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
